Source: flickos-control
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               python3
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: flickos-control
Architecture: all
# python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0: the window, GTK 3 so it follows the Arc theme.
# The pages run the commands that own the settings: flickos-layout (1.13
# merges the input fragment and the keyboard layout into its overlay, 1.19
# `state` reads the whole layout page at once, 1.22 records its changes for
# History and takes `default`, which History's undo runs, 1.37 merges the
# zoom settings' <magnifier>, 1.46 marks users' own styles and names the
# defaults in `state`), flick-tiler (1.3:
# floating, gap, ratio in status; 1.5 the same as flickos-layout 1.22),
# flickos-shortcuts.
# flickos-screenshot (1.6: get/set/state for the Screenshots page; History's
# undo runs set).
# pkexec, xkb-data: the system keyboard layout and autologin (control-helper).
# adduser: new user accounts (control-helper user-add; passwd has the rest).
# ufw is not a dependency: the Firewall page is left out without it.
# xdg-utils: default apps (xdg-mime).
# libglib2.0-bin: gsettings, the Animations switch (already in the image
# through flickos-layouts).
# kanshi, wlr-randr: kept screen arrangements (Displays). Depends, so
# installed systems get them; kanshi runs only while an arrangement is kept.
# locales (locale-gen, the list of languages) is a Recommends of
# flickos-desktop; without it the Language & Region page is left out.
Depends: python3,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         flickos-layouts (>= 1.46),
         flick-tiler (>= 1.5),
         flickos-shortcuts,
         flickos-screenshot (>= 1.6),
         pkexec,
         xkb-data,
         adduser,
         xdg-utils,
         libglib2.0-bin,
         kanshi,
         wlr-randr,
         ${misc:Depends}
# The Phone page's media row runs flickos-phone 1.13 (set media), its
# commands list 1.14 (commands list|add|remove), and Open Phone runs
# flickos-phone 1.16 (window).
Breaks: flickos-phone (<< 1.16)
# About: wl-copy for Copy System Info (else GTK's clipboard), lspci for the
# graphics card (else left out).
Recommends: wl-clipboard,
            pciutils
Description: Settings window of the FlickOS desktop
 One window for the settings of the FlickOS labwc desktop: desktop layout,
 style and desktop clicks, mouse and touchpad, keyboard layout and typing,
 window tiling, screen arrangements kept for every login and whenever the
 same screens are plugged in, night light, language and formats, the
 keyboard shortcuts, default applications, startup applications,
 screenshots and screen recordings, Do Not Disturb for
 notifications, screen lock and sleep times, the power
 button and the lid, date and time, automatic updates, logging in
 automatically, user accounts, the
 firewall on or off, the anonymous weekly count (while flickos-countme is
 installed), and what the system is (with a copy for bug reports).
 Other settings (wallpaper, appearance, arranging the screens, network,
 sound, Bluetooth, printers, software updates) open their own app from the
 same window.
 .
 Each page runs the FlickOS command that owns the setting, so a change made
 here is the same as one made in the panel, with a key or on the command
 line.
